{"uid":"6a3ddeff748155de","name":"test_criteria_edited_via_the_agent_readable_view_never_reaches_the_record","fullName":"tests.test_e2e#test_criteria_edited_via_the_agent_readable_view_never_reaches_the_record","historyId":"75044c237c526c563c3dc2b6f5d18f38","time":{"start":1791919432300,"stop":1791919433950,"duration":1650},"description":"Task 008 + task 024 (requirement E.3, #116 section 2) built the\n    detect-and-refuse machinery this test used to pin under the title\n    `..._is_refused` -- a task that fails verification once, then gets its\n    successCriteria rewritten by the worker instead of the actual work being\n    fixed. Task 004 (requirement B, #202) closes the vector this stub used to\n    reach the record at all: `STUB_REWRITE_CRITERIA` opens `tasks.json` (now\n    only the agent-readable VIEW copy, `run.tasks_file`) directly and\n    rewrites `successCriteria` in place -- exactly the shape a fully dropped\n    agent uid can still perform against that copy, since it is a courtesy\n    mirror, never trusted. `RunDir.read_tasks`/`read_tasks_result` read only\n    the protected copy, so this lands nowhere the engine ever looks: the run\n    proceeds exactly like `test_vigilant_verify_fail_then_recovery` above\n    (one retry, then both tasks validated), oblivious, and the persisted\n    record -- live and archived alike -- carries the ORIGINAL criteria\n    throughout. task 008/024's own detect-and-refuse marker\n    (`LoopSupervisor._check_criteria_edits`) is still very much alive --\n    `tests/test_criteria_fingerprint.py`/`test_contract_events.py` pin it\n    against a rewrite landed the one way that still reaches the record,\n    through `write_tasks()` itself -- this test just no longer has a way to\n    DEMONSTRATE that path, because the raw-file-write vector it used to use\n    no longer lands anywhere that matters.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 008 + task 024 (requirement E.3, #116 section 2) built the<br />\ndetect-and-refuse machinery this test used to pin under the title<br />\n<code>..._is_refused</code> -- a task that fails verification once, then gets its<br />\nsuccessCriteria rewritten by the worker instead of the actual work being<br />\nfixed. Task 004 (requirement B, #202) closes the vector this stub used to<br />\nreach the record at all: <code>STUB_REWRITE_CRITERIA</code> opens <code>tasks.json</code> (now<br />\nonly the agent-readable VIEW copy, <code>run.tasks_file</code>) directly and<br />\nrewrites <code>successCriteria</code> in place -- exactly the shape a fully dropped<br />\nagent uid can still perform against that copy, since it is a courtesy<br />\nmirror, never trusted. <code>RunDir.read_tasks</code>/<code>read_tasks_result</code> read only<br />\nthe protected copy, so this lands nowhere the engine ever looks: the run<br />\nproceeds exactly like <code>test_vigilant_verify_fail_then_recovery</code> above<br />\n(one retry, then both tasks validated), oblivious, and the persisted<br />\nrecord -- live and archived alike -- carries the ORIGINAL criteria<br />\nthroughout. task 008/024's own detect-and-refuse marker<br />\n(<code>LoopSupervisor._check_criteria_edits</code>) is still very much alive --<br />\n<code>tests/test_criteria_fingerprint.py</code>/<code>test_contract_events.py</code> pin it<br />\nagainst a rewrite landed the one way that still reaches the record,<br />\nthrough <code>write_tasks()</code> itself -- this test just no longer has a way to<br />\nDEMONSTRATE that path, because the raw-file-write vector it used to use<br />\nno longer lands anywhere that matters.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791919432281,"stop":1791919432287,"duration":6},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":